  "label": "Rainbow Flag",
  "description": "The rainbow flag is the most widely recognized symbol of LGBTQ+ Pride. It was designed by Gilbert Baker in 1969 and has since become an international emblem of LGBTQ+ identity, diversity, and solidarity. Its colors represent different aspects of the community (e.g., red for life, orange for healing, yellow for sunlight, green for nature, blue for harmony, and violet for spirit). Its presence in the image is a direct visual reference to LGBTQ+ Pride culture.",
